{
  "id": "Compound::DB00528 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Lercanidipine is shown to bind to Cyp3a7 and Cyp3a5, which are both members of the cytochrome P450 3A family. These enzymes are known to participate in the metabolism of various substrates, including estrogens and other xenobiotics. The observed pathway links Lercanidipine to Cyp3a4 through a series of enzymatic activities, including aromatase activity and oxidoreductase activity. This suggests that Lercanidipine may influence the metabolic activity of Cyp3a4, potentially affecting the conversion of substrates such as estrogens. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanistic link between Lercanidipine and Cyp3a4, where the drug's binding to Cyp3a7 and Cyp3a5 may modulate the activity of Cyp3a4, which is involved in the metabolism of multiple compounds. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism by which Lercanidipine could interact with Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
